---
const faqs = [
	{
		question: 'What does Zelavis replace?',
		answer: 'Zelavis combines the platform capabilities engineering teams usually stitch together from separate tools: backend-as-a-service (auth, database, real-time), CMS (schemas, entries, media), hosting control panels (domains, deployments, logs), and functions/workloads platforms. You can run the entire platform unified or embed specific subpaths.',
	},
	{
		question: 'Can I run it completely on my own infrastructure?',
		answer: 'Yes. Self-hosting is a foundational architectural requirement, not an afterthought or enterprise-only export. Zelavis is designed to host applications directly on your own VPS, bare-metal servers, or private cloud, with managed Zelavis Cloud offered as a seamless option.',
	},
	{
		question: 'Is Zelavis tied strictly to SQLite?',
		answer: 'No. The database storage engine operates over an ordered key-value boundary. While SQLite is the zero-config default, libSQL, RocksDB, and LMDB drivers are built in and operate behind the identical logical database API and multi-model projections.',
	},
	{
		question: 'Does a single-node setup still use the sharded architecture?',
		answer: 'Yes. Every official Zelavis App is physically and locally sharded from the moment of creation. On a single server, the virtual shard ranges simply colocate on one machine. When you scale horizontally, the platform moves shard placements rather than forcing an architectural rewrite.',
	},
	{
		question: 'Which parts are implemented and usable today?',
		answer: 'The core runtime, Node process isolation, multi-model document/column/measure/graph projections, authentication foundations, background workloads, official @zelavis/ui dashboard, and native server hosting are implemented. Real-time multiplayer collaboration and team issue planning are committed roadmap milestones.',
	},
];
---

<section class="amp-dark amp-faq" id="questions" data-local-content>
	<div class="amp-wrap faq-wrap">
		<div class="faq-head" data-reveal>
			<p class="amp-eyebrow">Clear answers</p>
			<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
			<p>Everything you need to know about self-hosting, architecture, and technology choices.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="faq-list" data-reveal>
			{faqs.map((faq, index) => (
				<details open={index === 0} class="faq-item">
					<summary class="faq-summary">
						<span>{faq.question}</span>
						<span class="faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true">
							<i></i><i></i>
						</span>
					</summary>
					<div class="faq-answer">
						<p>{faq.answer}</p>
					</div>
				</details>
			))}
		</div>

		<div class="faq-footer-cta" data-reveal>
			<p>Have questions about your specific stack or deployment?</p>
			<div class="faq-cta-links">
				<a href="/docs" class="faq-link">Browse Documentation →</a>
				<a href="https://github.com/zelavis/zelavis/discussions" class="faq-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Join Community Discussions →</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.amp-dark {
		background: #0d0e14;
		color: #f7f7f9;
	}

	.amp-faq {
		padding: 100px 0 160px;
	}

	.amp-wrap {
		width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 64px));
		margin: 0 auto;
	}

	.faq-wrap {
		max-width: 860px;
	}

	.faq-head {
		text-align: center;
		margin-bottom: 56px;
	}

	.amp-eyebrow {
		margin: 0 0 14px;
		font-size: 13px;
		line-height: 1.2;
		font-weight: 750;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: #a49aff;
	}

	.faq-head h2 {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: clamp(36px, 4.5vw, 52px);
		line-height: 1.1;
		letter-spacing: -0.035em;
		font-weight: 750;
		color: #fff;
	}

	.faq-head p:last-child {
		max-width: 600px;
		margin: 16px auto 0;
		font-size: 17px;
		line-height: 1.6;
		color: #9295a6;
	}

	.faq-list {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
	}

	.faq-item {
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
		transition: background 0.2s ease;
	}

	.faq-summary {
		padding: 24px 0;
		display: flex;
		justify-content: space-between;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 20px;
		cursor: pointer;
		font-size: 18px;
		font-weight: 650;
		color: #f0f2fa;
		list-style: none;
		user-select: none;
	}

	.faq-summary::-webkit-details-marker {
		display: none;
	}

	.faq-summary:hover {
		color: #fff;
	}

	.faq-toggle {
		position: relative;
		width: 20px;
		height: 20px;
		flex-shrink: 0;
	}

	.faq-toggle i {
		position: absolute;
		background: #a49aff;
		border-radius: 2px;
		transition: transform 0.25s ease;
	}

	.faq-toggle i:first-child {
		top: 9px;
		left: 2px;
		width: 16px;
		height: 2px;
	}

	.faq-toggle i:last-child {
		top: 2px;
		left: 9px;
		width: 2px;
		height: 16px;
	}

	.faq-item[open] .faq-toggle i:last-child {
		transform: rotate(90deg);
		opacity: 0;
	}

	.faq-answer {
		padding-bottom: 24px;
	}

	.faq-answer p {
		margin: 0;
		color: #9fa2b4;
		font-size: 15.5px;
		line-height: 1.68;
		max-width: 740px;
	}

	.faq-footer-cta {
		margin-top: 64px;
		padding: 32px;
		border-radius: 18px;
		background: #141622;
		border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
		text-align: center;
	}

	.faq-footer-cta p {
		margin: 0 0 16px;
		font-size: 15px;
		color: #cbd0e2;
	}

	.faq-cta-links {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: center;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 20px;
	}

	.faq-link {
		color: #a49aff;
		font-size: 14px;
		font-weight: 650;
		text-decoration: none;
		transition: color 0.18s ease;
	}

	.faq-link:hover {
		color: #c4bdff;
		text-decoration: underline;
	}

	@media (max-width: 640px) {
		.amp-faq {
			padding: 70px 0 110px;
		}

		.faq-summary {
			font-size: 16px;
			padding: 20px 0;
		}

		.faq-answer p {
			font-size: 14px;
		}

		.faq-cta-links {
			flex-direction: column;
			gap: 10px;
		}
	}
</style>
